# A reserved word as a column name: DS0126 with a fix that quotes it.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | extend null = 1, true = 2
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..41
  PIPELINE@0..40
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    EXTEND_OP@15..40
      IDENT@15..21 "extend"
      WHITESPACE@21..22 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@22..30
        NAME@22..26
          NULL_KW@22..26 "null"
        WHITESPACE@26..27 " "
        EQ@27..28 "="
        WHITESPACE@28..29 " "
        LITERAL@29..30
          LONG@29..30 "1"
      COMMA@30..31 ","
      WHITESPACE@31..32 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@32..40
        NAME@32..36
          TRUE_KW@32..36 "true"
        WHITESPACE@36..37 " "
        EQ@37..38 "="
        WHITESPACE@38..39 " "
        LITERAL@39..40
          LONG@39..40 "2"
  WHITESPACE@40..41 "\n"

error[DS0126]: `null` is a reserved word
  --> query:1:23
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | extend null = 1, true = 2
  |                       ^^^^ a reserved word cannot be a name without quotes
  |
  = help: to use it as a name, quote it: `['null']`

error[DS0126]: `true` is a reserved word
  --> query:1:33
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | extend null = 1, true = 2
  |                                 ^^^^ a reserved word cannot be a name without quotes
  |
  = help: to use it as a name, quote it: `['true']`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    'orders.csv' | extend ['null'] = 1, ['true'] = 2
which parses without errors
